09/28/26|09/28/26||PDT|0|F|Y|Natomas|CA|38.6507|-121.5067|OZONE|44|Good|No|Monday, an upper-level trough of low pressure will gradually move across the Sacramento Valley, promoting atmospheric mixing. Furthermore, mild temperatures will inhibit ozone production. Therefore, ozone levels will be Good.  Tuesday, sunny skies and temperatures in the low-90s will increase ozone development. However, moderate north-northwesterly winds across the Sacramento region will promote dispersion. As a result, ozone levels will be high-Good.  Wednesday, winds will weaken in the Sacramento region, reducing pollutant dispersion. Additionally, as an upper-level ridge of high pressure builds over northern California, sunny skies and temperatures in the low-90s will continue to support ozone formation, leading to low-Moderate AQI levels.|Sacramento Metro. AQMD
